}
```

### Component Implementation Pattern
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Multilingual sharing
const handleShareResult = async () => {
  if (!result) return;
  
  const resultTitle = result.title[locale as keyof typeof result.title] || result.title.ko;
  const shareMessage = t('optimismTest.shareMessages.default', { type: resultTitle });
  const shareText = `${shareMessage}\n\n${url}`;
  
  // ... rest of implementation
};

// ❌ WRONG - Hardcoded Korean text
const handleShareResult = async () => {
  const shareText = `나는 ${resultTitle}! 🌤️ 컵에 물이 반? 너는 어떻게 볼래?\n\n${url}`;
  // Korean text hardcoded
};
```

## Slug Management Rules (CRITICAL)

### 1. Slug Uniqueness Requirements
❌ DON'T:
- Overwrite existing slugs with new content
- Use the same slug for different tests
- Change existing slug mappings without explicit user permission
- Assume you can modify existing slug behavior

✅ DO:
- ALWAYS create new unique slugs for new tests
- Check existing slugs before creating new ones
- Ask user for explicit permission before modifying existing slugs
- Use descriptive, unique slug names that don't conflict

### 2. Slug Conflict Resolution
✅ DO follow this process:
1. **Check existing slugs first** - Search for similar slugs in the codebase
2. **Create unique slug** - If similar content exists, use a different slug name
3. **Ask user permission** - If you must modify existing slug, ask explicitly
4. **Document changes** - Clearly explain what slug changes were made

### 3. Slug Naming Convention
✅ DO use descriptive, unique names:
- `test-name-1`, `test-name-2` for similar tests
- `test-name-v2` for updated versions
- `test-name-extreme` for harder versions
- `test-name-advanced` for advanced versions

❌ DON'T reuse existing slugs:
- If `extreme-quiz` exists, don't use it for different content
- If `mensa-test` exists, don't overwrite it with new content
- Always create new slugs: `mensa-extreme`, `mensa-advanced`, etc.

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

1. **Hardcoding Korean in sharing functions** - Always use t() function
2. **Missing alert localizations** - All user-facing alerts must be localized
3. **Inconsistent message formats** - Keep message structure consistent across platforms
4. **Missing translation keys** - Ensure all 7 languages have complete keys
5. **Ignoring locale parameter** - Always check locale before displaying text
6. **Slug conflicts** - NEVER overwrite existing slugs without explicit permission
7. **Slug reuse** - Always create unique slugs for new content

## New Test Development Common Mistakes (CRITICAL)

### 1. Translation Key Path Errors
❌ DON'T:
- Use incorrect translation key paths like `t('testName.otherTest.ui.*')` when using `useTranslations('testName')`
- Mix translation namespaces incorrectly
- Use global keys without `tGlobal = useTranslations()`

✅ DO:
- When using `useTranslations('testName')`, call `t('ui.*')` not `t('testName.ui.*')`
- For global keys (like `mbti.*`), use `const tGlobal = useTranslations()` then `tGlobal('mbti.*')`
- Always verify translation key paths match the namespace structure

### 2. Translation Keys Exposed in UI
❌ DON'T:
- Leave missing translation keys in messages files
- Use translation keys that don't exist in all language files

✅ DO:
- Add ALL required translation keys to ALL 7 language files (ko, en, ja, zh-CN, zh-TW, vi, id)
- Verify keys exist before using them: `t('testName.ui.similarTests')` requires `testName.ui.similarTests` in all message files
- Check for missing keys in recommendations, alerts, and UI sections

### 3. Chinese Comma Separation Issues
❌ DON'T:
- Only split by English comma (`,`) and Japanese comma (`、`)
- Ignore Chinese comma (`，`) in characteristics/features data

✅ DO:
- Use `split(/[,、，]/)` to handle English, Japanese, and Chinese commas
- Test with Chinese simplified and traditional text to ensure proper splitting

### 4. Start Screen Title Multilingual Missing
❌ DON'T:
- Forget to create SQL file for new test
- Leave fallback data with empty multilingual fields
- Assume DB will have multilingual data without inserting it

✅ DO:
- ALWAYS create `supabase/insert-test-name.sql` file with complete multilingual data
- Include all 7 languages in title and description fields
- Run SQL file to insert data into database
- Verify fallback data in `page.tsx` has complete multilingual fields

### 5. Social Sharing Messages Missing for Start Screen
❌ DON'T:
- Only add result sharing messages (`shareMessages.default`, `shareMessages.kakao`, etc.)
- Forget start screen sharing messages

✅ DO:
- Add BOTH result and start screen sharing messages:
  ```json
  "shareMessages": {
    "default": "Result message...",
    "kakao": "Result message...",
    "startDefault": "Start screen message...",
    "startKakao": "Start screen message...",
    "startWechat": "Start screen message...",
    "startWhatsapp": "Start screen message...",
    "startTelegram": "Start screen message...",
    "startLine": "Start screen message..."
  }
  ```
- Update all sharing functions to use start messages when `result` is null

### 6. Result Screen Type Display Issues
❌ DON'T:
- Display only Type number (e.g., "Type 1", "Type 2")
- Show Type without emoji and title

✅ DO:
- Display Type with emoji and localized title:
  ```typescript
  const matchTitle = matchResult.title[locale as keyof typeof matchResult.title] || matchResult.title.ko;
  const matchEmoji = matchResult.emoji;
  // Display: {matchEmoji} {matchTitle}
  ```

### 7. Question/Answer Shuffling Score Calculation
❌ DON'T:
- Store scores using shuffled question indices
- Calculate results with shuffled order

✅ DO:
- Map shuffled questions to original indices: `originalQuestionIndices`
- Store scores using original question indices: `answers[originalIndex] = score`
- Reconstruct answers array in original order before calculation:
  ```typescript
  const answersArray = questions.map((_, idx) => answers[idx] ?? 0);
  const resultType = calculateResult(answersArray);
  ```

### 8. Font Size and Alignment Issues
❌ DON'T:
- Use oversized fonts (e.g., `fontSize: '1.5em'`) for section data
- Mix alignment styles inconsistently

✅ DO:
- Use normal font size for section data
- Left-align section titles: `text-left`
- Center-align section data: `justify-center` or `text-center`
- Add emojis to section titles: `📊 공감 지수`, `⭐ 주요 특징`

### 9. Characteristics Section Styling
❌ DON'T:
- Display characteristics as plain text
- Ignore visual separation of multiple characteristics

✅ DO:
- Split characteristics by comma: `split(/[,、，]/)`
- Display each characteristic in a rounded box:
  ```typescript
  {characteristics.split(/[,、，]/).map((char, idx) => (
    <span key={idx} className="inline-block bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-100 to-pink-100 text-purple-800 text-sm font-semibold px-3 py-1 rounded-full shadow-sm">
      {char.trim()}
    </span>
  ))}
  ```

### 10. Multilingual Translation Order
❌ DON'T:
- Try to translate all 7 languages at once
- Start multilingual translation before Korean version is complete and tested

✅ DO:
- Complete Korean version first
- Test functionality thoroughly with Korean version
- Then translate to other languages one by one or in small batches
- Verify each language works before moving to next

### 11. SQL File Creation Checklist
✅ DO create SQL file with:
- [ ] Complete multilingual title (7 languages)
- [ ] Complete multilingual description (7 languages)
- [ ] Correct thumbnail filename
- [ ] Correct type and category values
- [ ] Complete multilingual tags (7 languages)
- [ ] `ON CONFLICT` clause for updates
- [ ] Test the SQL file before committing

### 12. Component Development Checklist
✅ DO verify:
- [ ] Translation key paths are correct for namespace
- [ ] All UI text uses translation keys
- [ ] All sharing functions handle both result and start screen cases
- [ ] Question shuffling preserves score calculation
- [ ] Result display shows emoji and localized titles
- [ ] Characteristics are properly styled and split
- [ ] Font sizes and alignments are consistent
- [ ] All 7 languages have complete translation keys
- [ ] SQL file is created and ready to run